acceptance_criteria: "Rank lexical relevance, recency and standing guidance; entire packets stay within budget; process-concurrent recall counters; random-set property tests and packer revert proof."
parent: pm-memory-0kwy
comments[44]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T13:32:34.261Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: revert only the packer acceptance predicate so oversized rows are accepted. npm run build passes; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"budget packer\" test/memory.test.ts fails with AssertionError and exit 1. Restoring the predicate passes. Two independent processes start behind a shared barrier and produce exactly six recall increments."
  "2026-10-19T13:41:19.814Z",codex-agent,"Accepted aggregate recall packets stay under 800 estimated tokens. Four preselected references appeared at ranks 1, 1, 1 and 3; the release-workflow reference was omitted from its three returned rows. This budget tradeoff is documented rather than hidden. Index: 1498 of 1500 tokens. Random-set property and synchronized process-counter tests passed."
  "2026-10-19T14:00:52.642Z",codex-agent,"Recall now packs compact scored rows first, preserves top rank at small budgets, spends spare space on marked excerpts, and exposes full content via memory get. Ranking includes descriptions and slugs. Regression covers huge top bodies at budgets 200 and 800."
  "2026-10-19T14:07:42.329Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: reverting only recall to the review baseline makes the 200-token top-1 regression fail (1 failed, 0 passed): a smaller fallback replaces the oversized highest-ranked memory. Restored code returns the top row and passes the focused suite."
  "2026-10-19T14:17:19.838Z",codex-agent,"Private ranking review exposed equal title/description weighting that buried a relevant reference. Adjusted weights to title 5, description 2, slug 1.5, other text 1; added a synthetic field-priority regression. Final five-query rank measurements pending."
  "2026-10-19T14:30:09.655Z",codex-agent,"Final private proof at budgets 800 and 200: reference ranks are 1,1,1,1,2 for the five prescribed queries at both budgets. Baseline replay ranks in packets were 1,1,omitted,1,2. Compact rows at 800 increased from 3 to 13; all packets fit, top-1 synthetic regression passes at 200. Index uses 1476/1500 estimated tokens. Aggregate table recorded in README."
  "2026-10-19T15:15:43.292Z",codex-agent,"Release-gate regression: scoring sampled Date.now independently for each memory. Advancing time during a ranking pass can incorrectly break a score tie before the slug tie-breaker. Capture one timestamp per pass; a real SDK memory plus a controlled advancing clock proves that equal-timestamp memories keep stable slug order. No SDK mocks."
  "2026-10-19T15:16:35.412Z",codex-agent,"Clock regression proof: the advancing-clock fixture passes with one timestamp per scoring pass, and fails with only scored reverted to b958419 (beta incorrectly precedes alpha). Both the direct and pm-linked regression pass after restoration. This removes the timing-dependent ranking failure without changing the tie contract."
  "2026-10-19T15:20:04.485Z",codex-agent,"Final verification: the advancing-clock regression is included in both isolated release gates, each passing 93/93 suite tests plus 2/2 packed npx/bunx consumers with 100/100/100/100 coverage. The scoring-only revert fails the regression; restored implementation passes. Release-gate timing failure resolved."
  "2026-10-21T14:39:32.039Z",codex-agent,"Extend existing recall with opt-in localhost Ollama embeddings, content-addressed runtime vectors, documented hybrid weights, budgeted lexical fallback notes, preview-only semantic duplicate proposals and a labelled synthetic retrieval benchmark. Preserve default lexical scores and pinned SDK version. Verify non-git execution, behavioural revert and unchanged npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-21T14:47:57.014Z",codex-agent,"Implemented loopback-only Ollama provider, deterministic no-model adapter and model-digest plus content-hash vector cache under runtime. Default stays lexical; explicit hybrid uses 30% normalized lexical score and 70% nonnegative cosine. Auto notes are included in token accounting. Synthetic corpus has 64 memories and 64 labelled queries. Initial embeddinggemma-2 measurement: lexical recall@1 0.203125, recall@5 0.5, MRR 0.332508; hybrid 0.28125, 0.625, 0.435186. These are full-ranking evaluation results, not budgeted or held-out generalization claims. Additional installed-model measurement and unchanged gates remain in progress."
  "2026-10-21T14:53:02.303Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: replacing only hybridScored with the pre-feature lexical ranking makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"hybrid ranking promotes paraphrases\" test/semantic.test.ts fail (0 passed, 1 failed; unrelated lexical hit precedes OIDC). Restoring hybridScored passes (1 passed, 0 failed). Tests import TypeScript source directly. Added published model-card query/document prompts and bumped cache input version to v2. Final measured embeddinggemma-2 hybrid recall@1 0.28125, recall@5 0.671875, MRR 0.442726 versus lexical 0.203125, 0.5, 0.332508. Qwen benchmark and independent embedding probe timed out; no Qwen quality claim."
  "2026-10-21T15:02:25.840Z",codex-agent,"Final design uses direct node:http requests to bypass environment proxies, loopback origin validation, installed local-model checks and model-card query/document prompts. Cache includes a private ignore rule for custom tracker locations. Semantic consolidation stays advisory and refuses apply before writes. Non-git regression removes Git from PATH and blocks ancestor discovery. Isolated health passes; normal-home health reports global pm-github host-version skew against the unchanged pinned host. Existing wall-clock privacy probe failed once under shared load; limits remain unchanged. Linked semantic test timeout is now 600 seconds to accommodate observed host contention."
  "2026-10-21T15:16:02.758Z",codex-agent,"Review found and fixed a direct-adapter SDK bypass: OllamaProvider.embed now revalidates an installed local model on every call, including calls outside recall, and refuses a changed revision before sending text. Regression confirms cloud aliases and retagged models receive no embedding inputs. Earlier CI at the first feature commit passed 184/184 tests, 2/2 packed consumers and 100/100/100/100 coverage on Node 22/26, including bun run release:check. Superseded the local run after this safety correction; final-head gates are rerunning."
  "2026-10-21T15:18:44.735Z",codex-agent,"Adapter guard behavioural revert proof: removing only the pre-request identity/revision checks from OllamaProvider.embed makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"local adapter validates\" test/semantic.test.ts fail (0 passed, 1 failed; missing expected retagging refusal). Restoring the checks passes (1 passed, 0 failed). Focused adapter/cache/ranking suite: 5/5 passed with 100/100/100/100 coverage for src/embeddings.ts. No encoding, ranking weights or benchmark labels changed."
  "2026-10-21T15:24:12.129Z",codex-agent,"Final source head 822e4f5 passed CI on Node 22 and Node 26, including the direct-adapter guard. Each full suite passed 184/184 tests with 100/100/100/100 coverage across 22 source files, and packed npm/Bun acceptance passed 2/2. Node 26 also passed bun run release:check at unchanged thresholds. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions/runs/39624570740 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/5. Local isolated npm run release:check remains in progress. Benchmark limitations remain explicit: small synthetic evaluation, one regressed query, motivating query rank unchanged, and no measured Qwen quality because of timeouts."
  "2026-10-21T15:45:52.144Z",codex-agent,"Final validation at source head 822e4f5: isolated npm run release:check passed all gates, 184/184 suite tests and 2/2 packed npm/Bun consumers; 22 intended source files measured at 100/100/100/100; production audit found zero vulnerabilities. CI Node 22 and Node 26 passed, including bun run release:check with the same counts and thresholds. Two behavioural reverts failed their targeted regressions, and both restored versions passed. Existing wall-clock privacy probes passed in the final local run. Public PR body and automated summaries were inspected for local paths; runtime/cache/build/dependency files are untracked. Follow-up pm-memory-qgiq records secondary-model availability and measurement. No pm CLI/SDK defect was established; normal-home health flags an external extension version skew while isolated health passes. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/5 remains open; no merge or release. Leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-21T15:52:33.386Z",codex-agent,"Final tracking head 2a8fd43 passed CI on Node 22 and Node 26, including the Bun release gate; isolated tracker health and identity checks pass. Executable source is unchanged from tested source head 822e4f5. External review evidence remains incomplete: Cubic returned a neutral quota-limit result, and no approval review is recorded. Maintainer/orchestrator review remains pending. Technical gates, measured benchmark results and both revert proofs remain valid; the item stays in progress and unclaimed for verification."
  "2026-10-21T16:18:24.839Z",codex-agent,"PR #5 review round: verified unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u2YPE. Capture consolidation corpus and lexical proposals under the writer lock, release before loopback embedding HTTP requests, preserve advisory output and lexical apply semantics. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Self-review also found semantic recall holds the same lock during embedding; fix that instance while preserving atomic emitted-only counters and retrying changed corpus snapshots. Add slow-loopback concurrency regressions and function-only revert proofs; run unchanged npm and Bun release gates with isolated Git identity."
  "2026-10-21T16:22:51.966Z",codex-agent,"Implemented review thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u2YPE and same-class recall correction. Slow loopback fixture withholds both embedding batches for a 17-memory preview while separate writer processes complete; lexical proposals and captured corpus remain stable and durable bytes change only from those writers. Recall releases the lock for document and query embeddings, retries insertions and content revisions, and atomically increments current counters without retrying counter-only drift. Typecheck, lint and zero-duplication checks passed. Function-only consolidate revert fails its targeted regression (0 passed, 1 failed, exit 1: writer blocked while embedding response is withheld); restored implementation passes (1 passed, 0 failed). Function-only recall revert fails with the same contention assertion (0 passed, 1 failed, exit 1). Final restored recall proof and full unchanged-threshold release gates follow."
  "2026-10-21T16:23:15.495Z",codex-agent,"Completed both behavioural revert proofs against PR head 57e4a58: replace only consolidate with its original function and node --test --test-name-pattern=\"semantic preview releases\" test/semantic.test.ts fails 0/1 with the withheld-response writer assertion; restoration passes 1/1. Replace only recall and node --test --test-name-pattern=\"semantic recall releases\" test/semantic.test.ts likewise fails 0/1; restoration passes 1/1, including insertion/edit retries and counter-only concurrency during a blocked query embedding. Tests execute TypeScript sources directly. All functions are restored; no thresholds or dependency pins changed. Full release checks are next."
  "2026-10-21T16:33:20.394Z",codex-agent,"Initial isolated npm release gate completed the suite at 185/186 with only the existing adversarial JWT privacy scanner exceeding its unchanged 500ms wall-clock assertion during host load. Both new concurrency regressions passed; all measured coverage dimensions were 100%, but the failed gate invalidated its reports. Immediate unchanged-limit retry with node --test --test-name-pattern=\"privacy scans adversarial JWT\" test/review-r1.test.ts passed 1/1. No scanner, deadline, gate threshold or test exemption was changed. Rerunning complete npm and Bun release gates; tracker strict health passes with one advisory queued-telemetry warning. Existing development dependency advisory remains tracked separately in pm-memory-eafx."
  "2026-10-21T16:39:54.772Z",codex-agent,"Verified source commit d1f105cc1c95a5b4c881a151a7f8d0a33c19f94b in CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions/runs/39635936425: Node 22 and Node 26 passed every npm release-check component, each with 186/186 suite tests and 2/2 packed npm/Bun consumers. Node 26 also ran bun run release:check successfully with 186/186 suite tests and 2/2 consumers. Each measured 22 intended source files at 100/100/100/100, zero duplication and zero production vulnerabilities; all 96 declarations documented. The existing local JWT privacy wall-clock failure passed its immediate focused retry and all CI executions. A redundant local full npm retry was stopped after complete source-head CI success; it is not claimed as a passing local gate. No test, timing limit, coverage threshold, dependency pin, lock policy or tracked build-output policy was weakened. Review inventory refreshed: exactly one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u2YPE; no outside-diff findings in the latest CodeRabbit review. Whole-diff review fixed the recall instance too and corrected stale architecture text. No thread replies, resolutions, mentions, merge or release. No new pm CLI/SDK defect was established. Open limits: continuously changing corpus content can delay recall retries; the existing development-only glob advisory remains tracked in pm-memory-eafx. Leave the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-21T17:24:26.656Z",codex-agent,"PR #5 review round: synchronized remote branch; base is already included. Fetched all review threads and comments with complete pagination receipts. Four unresolved findings are valid: benchmark cache isolation, skip semantic consolidation for fewer than two active memories, separate lexical relevance from pin/age priors, and single-read lexical recall. Latest CodeRabbit review has no additional outside-diff findings. Plan regression and behavioral revert proof per finding, whole-diff review, unchanged npm and Bun release gates, then commit and push without resolving threads."
  "2026-10-21T17:27:20.619Z",codex-agent,"Implemented all four verified review fixes. Behavioral revert proofs against b0343d7: reverting only runBench (using the equivalent joined tracker path) fails benchmark entrypoint isolates; reverting only semanticProposals fails semantic consolidation skips with model unavailable; reverting only scored/hybridScored fails hybrid priors benchmark (recall@1 0.5 and MRR 0.75 instead of 1.0); reverting only recall fails lexical recall uses one (two corpus reads instead of one). Each command was node --test --test-name-pattern=\"<named prefix>\" test/semantic.test.ts: individually 0 passed/1 failed, exit 1. Restored implementations pass all four regressions together, 4 passed/0 failed. Source imports mean no dist rebuild is needed for these proofs. No dist files are tracked. Whole-diff review confirmed both embedding callers skip their unusable corpus sizes and both recall modes share packet/counter updates. Controlled pin/age benchmark selects prior coefficient 0.01 with maximum hybrid prior contribution 0.007; legacy lexical scores are unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T17:40:14.102Z",codex-agent,"Focused linked review regressions pass 4/4. Type checking, identity/privacy, lint, zero duplication, all 97 docstrings across 22 source files, generated changelog and isolated strict tracker health pass. Full isolated npm release gate is still running without a reported failure under host contention; push the stable implementation to obtain complete npm/Bun CI evidence concurrently. Historical model benchmark is explicitly labelled as preceding the prior correction; the new controlled pin/age benchmark measures the corrected production ranker."
  "2026-10-21T17:44:25.021Z",codex-agent,"Initial CI release attempt caught test contamination in the new benchmark regression: stacking two mocks on OllamaProvider.embed left the first replacement installed after restoreAll. The four new focused tests passed, but later semantic tests failed with the leaked vectors. Replaced the nested mock with mockImplementation on one mock context so cleanup restores the actual adapter. Stopped the obsolete local npm run after reproducing the same later semantic failures; it is not counted as a successful release gate. Run the entire semantic test file and fresh unchanged release gates before final verification."
  "2026-10-21T17:45:53.891Z",codex-agent,"The sixth initial CI failure was an existing CLI assertion made obsolete by the requested singleton fast path: a one-memory semantic consolidation now correctly returns without a fallback note. The non-git CLI regression now checks the singleton result, then inserts a second memory and checks unavailable-model lexical fallback. Five other failures were caused by the nested embedding mock and are addressed by a single mock context. No production threshold, timeout or dependency changed."
  "2026-10-21T17:59:44.150Z",codex-agent,"Final source verification at 125bde6: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions/runs/39646810335 passes all npm release-check components on Node 22 and 26, each with 190/190 suite tests and 2/2 packed npm/Bun consumers. Node 26 also passes bun run release:check with 190/190 and 2/2. Every run measures all 22 intended source files at 100/100/100/100; duplication is zero; all 97 declarations are documented; production audit has zero vulnerabilities. Repeated all four behavioral reverts against b0343d7 after the test-isolation correction: each matched regression fails 0 passed/1 failed, restored suite passes 4/4. Corrected non-git singleton-plus-pair CLI regression passes 1/1. An unchanged 10-second writer deadline failed once in the loaded local pm-linked preview test, while the direct retry and all final CI runs pass. Obsolete local runs and the redundant final npm/Bun launcher stopped after CI success are not counted as passing local gates. Latest review inventory still has exactly the four requested threads and no outside-diff findings. All four are valid and fixed; no replies, thread resolutions, mentions, merge or release. No new pm CLI/SDK bug established. Existing development-only advisory is tracked by pm-memory-eafx; continuous content changes can still delay semantic recall retries. Leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-21T19:16:29.203Z",codex-agent,"PR 5 review round: fetched every unresolved thread and all comments with no remaining pagination; latest CodeRabbit body has five inline findings and no separate outside-diff or nitpick findings. All five verified: revision drift across benchmark queries, repeated pairwise norms, inherited HTTP proxy agent, untagged model lookup, and assertion deadline below writer wait. Whole-diff review additionally found repeated query norms in recall, now shared through unit-vector helpers. Local validation limited to targeted regressions, typecheck and lint; unchanged npm and Bun full gates delegated to CI. Branch current and not behind main. Dependency installation completed; two tracker writes that could not start during installation are retried here."
  "2026-10-21T19:18:21.755Z",codex-agent,"Initial focused regression run passes 5/5; npm run typecheck and npm run lint both pass. Tests use real plain-directory trackers and SDK operations; only local embedding protocol responses are synthetic. Proxy test uses a real child process with NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1, both HTTP proxy variable cases set to an unreachable endpoint and empty NO_PROXY. Canonicalization includes registry-port names and explicit tags. Norm operation budget covers consolidation and recall. Fake-clock test spans the entire writer wait and checks eventual rejection and completion cleanup. No release thresholds, dependency pins or production deadlines changed."
  "2026-10-21T19:19:27.455Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs against 9cf07c1: replacing only benchmark, semanticProposals, hybridScored, OllamaProvider.request, OllamaProvider.constructor, or whileEmbedding with the previous function makes its corresponding targeted regression fail (each exit 1, 0 passed/1 failed). All other fixes and regressions remain present. Benchmark fails with Missing expected rejection; consolidation fails its linear norm budget; recall fails query norm reuse; proxy test fails with ECONNREFUSED to the configured proxy; constructor fails because untagged names lack :latest; fake-clock deadline test fails because it settles before the entire writer wait. Sources restored in finally after each proof. No build needed because tests import TypeScript sources. Thread mapping: PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u6Jux benchmark revision guard; PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u6Ju- unit vectors before pair comparisons; PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u6JvM dedicated direct HTTP agent; PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u6JvU canonical model tags including registry ports; PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u6Jve 45-second assertion deadline. Additional self-review fix: hybridScored reuses document and query norms. No invalid findings. Threads were neither replied to nor resolved."
  "2026-10-21T19:21:11.758Z",codex-agent,"Restored fixes pass 5/5 via the linked regression command using pm test pm-memory-lc64 --run --only-last --progress (only new linked test index 6 executed; older linked commands intentionally not run locally). A final constructor revert using explicit canonical-name fixtures also fails 0/1 as expected. Final npm run typecheck and npm run lint pass. Tracker test-result persistence is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment records the sanitized results without changing that policy. No load-related test timeout occurred this round. Full npm and Bun release gates await CI; no committed dist files exist, and source-importing regressions require no build."
  "2026-10-21T19:23:21.184Z",codex-agent,"Pre-push checks: npm run changelog:full and npm run changelog:check pass. Native local strict health refused only because a globally installed pm-github extension requires a newer host than this repository pins. Repeating strict health with a fresh home and isolated global Git configuration passes all 10 checks; repository dependency pins and global settings remain unchanged. One pending telemetry queue entry is advisory and no telemetry configuration was changed. Added-line privacy inspection found no private path or topology literals. CI will establish fresh-clone full-gate evidence."
  "2026-10-21T19:33:18.729Z",codex-agent,"Implementation head 59713f0dc14e0e9f94737869acb79d2923fea5c2 passes CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions/runs/39661305149 : every npm release-check component passes on Node 22 and 26 with 195/195 suite tests and 2/2 packed npm/Bun consumers per job. Node 26 also passes bun run release:check with 195/195 tests and 2/2 packed consumers. Coverage is 100% statements, branches, functions and lines across all 22 intended source files; duplication is zero; docstring gate documents 97 declarations; production audit reports zero vulnerabilities. Strict tracker health, identity/privacy, changelog and release-publish attestation checks pass. Thresholds, dependency pins and production deadlines remain unchanged. Six isolated function reverts each fail 0/1, while restored targeted regressions pass 5/5. No load-related test timeout occurred. Existing development-only dependency exposure remains separately tracked. Final whole-diff review and fresh review fetch found no additional review findings; no threads replied to or resolved. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification, leaving status in_progress. An evidence-only commit will carry this receipt and will itself be checked in CI."
  "2026-10-21T20:24:50.932Z",codex-agent,"PR 5 current review: remote head synchronized and main already included. Complete review-thread and comment pagination confirms four unresolved findings, all valid: shared benchmark weights, semantic pair age direction, per-input embedding rejection isolation, and bounded semantic recall retries. Latest CodeRabbit body has no additional outside-diff findings. Plan targeted regressions and isolated behavioral revert proofs, whole-diff review for matching classes, typecheck and lint locally, and unchanged full npm/Bun release gates in CI. No replies, resolutions, mentions, merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T20:27:49.907Z",codex-agent,"Implemented PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u7qQ3 with immutable shared production/benchmark weights; PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u7qRB with ascending age and slug ordering; PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u7qRH with typed HTTP 400/413 document rejection, per-input retries, healthy-vector caching, zero-cosine recall and omitted semantic pairs; PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u7qRM with five bounded content-conflict attempts and a conflict remedy. Whole-diff review covers both vector consumers, query/model/daemon strict failures, both recall modes and the separately deadline-bounded writer wait. SDK exports the input-rejection type. Documentation reflects the resulting behavior. Targeted checks pass 10/10; initial score assertions were stabilized using fixed time and identical arithmetic ordering, without changing production behavior or thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T20:27:52.515Z",codex-agent,"Seven behavioral revert proofs against 09ac301: revert only benchmark -> shared-weight regression fails; semanticProposals -> pair-order regression fails; memoryVectors -> rejection regression fails; OllamaProvider.request -> rejection regression fails; hybridScored -> rejection regression fails; semanticProposals -> rejection-consumer regression fails; recall -> bounded-conflict regression fails with missing expected rejection. Each command was node --test --test-name-pattern=\"<matching review test prefix>\" test/semantic.test.ts, each exited 1 with 0 passed and 1 failed. All other fixes and all new tests remained present; source functions restored after each run. No build needed: tests import TypeScript sources directly, and dist is not tracked."
  "2026-10-21T20:29:15.973Z",codex-agent,"Exact revert commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^review benchmark reports\" test/semantic.test.ts for benchmark; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^review semantic pairs\" test/semantic.test.ts for semanticProposals age ordering; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^review rejected documents\" test/semantic.test.ts independently for memoryVectors, OllamaProvider.request, hybridScored and semanticProposals missing-vector handling; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^review semantic recall stops\" test/semantic.test.ts for recall. Each isolated revert yields 0 passed/1 failed, exit 1. Restored linked command passes 10/10 through pm test pm-memory-lc64 --run --only-last --progress. Final npm run typecheck and npm run lint pass. No host-load timeout occurred this round. Full npm and Bun release checks are delegated to CI at unchanged thresholds; no dependency pins or production deadlines changed. No new pm CLI/SDK bug established. Existing development advisory remains tracked separately in pm-memory-eafx."
  "2026-10-21T20:35:45.251Z",codex-agent,"Implementation head fcd89534891285806576203919ea65309d65a61b passes CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions/runs/39670766463 : Node 22 and 26 each pass all npm release-check components with 200/200 suite tests and 2/2 packed npm/Bun consumers. Node 26 also passes bun run release:check with 200/200 tests and 2/2 packed consumers. Each measures all 22 intended source files at 100% statements, branches, functions and lines; duplication is zero across 52 measured sources; all 98 declarations are documented; production audit reports zero vulnerabilities. Strict tracker health, identity/privacy, generated changelog and publish-attestation checks pass. CodeQL passes. Thresholds, dependency pins and production deadlines remain unchanged. Seven function-only reverts fail 0/1 each and restored linked targeted checks pass 10/10; local typecheck and lint pass. No load-related timeout occurred. No new pm CLI/SDK bug established. Existing development-only advisory remains tracked separately; rejected documents may retry on later calls and semantic preview remains pairwise. No replies, resolutions, mentions, merge or release. Release the claim while leaving status in_progress for orchestrator verification; a tracker-only receipt commit will itself run CI."
  "2026-10-21T22:49:24.010Z",codex-agent,"PR 5 review round: synchronized remote head 7263619; main is already included. Complete GraphQL thread and comment pagination confirms only PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u-he2 is unresolved. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff or nitpick findings. Verified the raw environment model expectation falsely fails untagged names; canonicalize the assertion and add isolated child-process environment cases. Whole PR diff checked for raw/canonical model comparisons and environment leakage; no other matching instance. Targeted regressions, behavior-only assertion revert proof, typecheck and lint run locally; full unchanged npm and Bun release gates run in CI. No thread replies, resolutions, mentions, merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T22:51:31.272Z",codex-agent,"Fixed the default provider assertion to canonicalize the configured name using a tag colon after the last slash. Added a child-process regression that runs the actual protocol test under six isolated environments: unset, untagged, namespaced, registry-port untagged, tagged, and registry-port tagged. The first regression attempt exposed inherited NODE_TEST_CONTEXT suppressing child output; reuse the existing testEnvironment helper to clear runner context while retaining coverage. Restored focused checks pass 3/3, with all six child protocol runs passing 1/1 each. npm run typecheck and npm run lint pass. No local host-load timeout occurred; dependencies installed successfully under shared-host contention. Production behavior, thresholds, dependency pins and deadlines are unchanged; dist files are not tracked."
  "2026-10-21T22:51:37.646Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof against 7263619: restore only the old raw-environment assertion inside the protocol test, leaving the new regression and production code unchanged. Exact command: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^default model assertion accepts\" test/semantic.test.ts. It exits 1 with 0 passed/1 failed; the embeddinggemma environment child reports actual embeddinggemma:latest versus expected embeddinggemma. The unset environment child first passes. Restored the two-line canonical assertion in finally. Tests import TypeScript sources; no build is required for this assertion-only proof."
